-996c-4194-b037-4f3234d02942"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete in the assigned worktree (uncommitted): extracted scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py, thinned the GitHub wrapper, added Jenkins/GitLab native wrappers, vendored the pinned GitLab Draft-07 schema with independently verified SHA-256/provenance, pinned shellcheck-py 0.11.0.1, retargeted continuity tests, and updated user/release docs. Validation: visible happy-path RED (5 expected failures) then GREEN (5 passed) in one implementation attempt; focused compatibility/policy suite 153 passed; make lint, make typecheck, make config-check, uv lock --check, actionlint, offline GitLab schema validation, and ShellCheck 0.11.0 provider-body checks all pass. No commit or push was made.","timestamp":1786419172169015001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Scope refinement from operator: the runner-neutral bridge capability must be available through all three public surfaces (Python library, CLI, MCP) and from all supported install paths (pip wheel, Homebrew's wheel-backed formula environment, and MCP Registry/uvx install). Preserve scripts/run_reconcile_bridge.py as a compatibility shim for checked-out workflows; provider wrappers should use an installed package entrypoint so clients do not need an unshipped repository script. Add RED-first interface-parity and wheel-content/install-path contract coverage before implementation.","timestamp":1786420192565397001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final pre-push validation: refreshed execution-phase plan review PASS (0 blocking). Advisory G1G2 is fixed in scope: tests that pinned the removed inline GitHub case/delivery shell were retargeted to assert delegation to the installed `rebar bridge run` seam while preserving routing, history, delivery, and policy behavior; the broader workflow/policy group is green. P4 size advisory is accepted because the 38 paths are one coherent cross-surface/install-path vertical slice and largely comprise held-out tests, generated references, provider contracts, and documentation. P6 compound-criterion advisory is accepted because the held-out suite asserts the constituent outcomes independently. Final gates: make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; make config-check PASS; uv lock --check PASS; git diff --check PASS; runner/library/CLI/MCP/provider/install-path held-out suite 65 passed. Residual-gap sweep: CLI, MCP, library, automated GitHub/GitLab/Jenkins callers, and bidirectional reconciler routing are fixed and proven in scope; contention testing is accepted as not applicable because the runner composes existing locked seams without retry/cache/check-then-act logic; no deferred review finding or hold-out compromise remains.","timestamp":1786423229130684001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 1595 after fetching and rebasing onto current origin/main. Patchset commit 397c8057d4; local post-rebase lint, typecheck, 65-test held-out suite, diff check, and commit-ticket verification all pass. Awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 before submit/close.","timestamp":1786423343298998001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit patchset 1 CI found the raw-git-write static gate could not resolve the generic subprocess helper argv. Confirmed RED with scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py; the helper only receives the closed rebar route table or sys.executable delivery command, never git. Added the required inline raw-git-ok rationale, then exact gate GREEN, lint/typecheck GREEN, and focused runner suite 28 passed. Amended same Change-Id, fetched origin/main again (0 behind), and pushed patchset 2 to change 1595.","timestamp":1786423611317366001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit PS2 default suite exposed two Linux-only test-fixture defects: the provider matrix included /usr/bin (where gh is installed), and the strict-delivery subprocess inherited pytest's autouse REBAR_ROOT sandbox instead of its disposable checkout. CI supplied RED evidence on 3 Linux versions. Fixed the fixtures without weakening production: isolated PATH now contains only explicit bash/git/fake-rebar; strict delivery pins REBAR_ROOT to its test checkout. Exact six cases GREEN, expanded runner/provider group 67 passed, lint/typecheck/raw-git gate/diff check green. Amended same Change-Id, fetched origin/main (0 behind), pushed PS3.","timestamp":1786425366397418001}],"created_at":1786404919211116001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"12554d17-f1c4-46db-aa69-6f227281cc94","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cf7d-fbf8-bd99-49e4"},{"link_uuid":"5fe79022-ed58-4e6a-a88f-be371a81803e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2b38-f76e-99eb-4d7d"}],"description":"## Context\n\nExtract bridge orchestration into a runner-neutral packaged Python core and keep provider workflows thin. The capability must work through all three public interfaces: Python library, CLI, and MCP. It must ship from all supported install paths: pip wheel, Homebrew's wheel-backed environment, and MCP Registry/uvx.\n\nThis is an additive migration. Existing checked-out workflows and environments that invoke `rebar reconcile --mode ...` keep their defaults, messages, mutation boundaries, and legacy benign results 3/4/75. At the provider boundary, the existing `MODE` environment variable remains supported; the new public operation uses the canonical noun `profile`.\n\nThe packaged runner accepts five profiles and preserves these routes:\n\n- `reconcile-check` invokes `rebar reconcile --mode reconcile-check`.\n- `dry-run` invokes `rebar bridge preview`.\n- `bootstrap-strict` invokes `rebar bridge sync --max-changes 10`.\n- `bootstrap-throttle` invokes `rebar bridge sync --max-changes 100`.\n- `live` invokes uncapped `rebar bridge sync`.\n\nThe Python core owns environment validation, the 3600-second timeout, pause-marker validation, provider-result translation, and strict ticket-store delivery. Direct legacy callers continue to observe 3/4/75; only the new provider runner maps benign legacy results to canonical success. GitHub Actions, Jenkins, and GitLab retain only provider-native checkout/bootstrap, credentials, signing-key materialization, artifacts/notifications, scheduling, and invocation of exactly `rebar bridge run`.\n\nGitLab portability is validated offline against a vendored Draft-07 schema with immutable upstream revision, retrieval date, dialect, and SHA-256 provenance. Shell embedded in provider configuration is linted with the exact pinned ShellCheck development dependency. No repository-local shell or Python runner script is shipped: behavior is in the wheel.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Inventory the existing workflow, compatibility contracts, and all parser/lint/policy consumers.\n2. Add RED-first happy, edge, end-to-end, surface-parity, and install-path tests; physically hold edge and end-to-end tests away from the implementation worker.\n3. Implement a packaged Python runner and expose it through `rebar.bridge_run`, `rebar bridge run --profile`, and a write-gated MCP `bridge_run` tool.\n4. Replace inline GitHub orchestration with the installed CLI and add native GitLab and Jenkins adapters that invoke the same CLI.\n5. Preserve provider `MODE` compatibility and direct legacy reconcile result behavior.\n6. Validate wheel contents and simulate pip, Homebrew wheel-backed, and MCP/uvx installations outside the repository.\n7. Validate provider schemas and embedded shell, then update generated references and user/release documentation.\n8. Run focused held-out suites, mutation checks, lint, typecheck, configuration checks, lock validation, and CI.\n\nNo contention harness is required: the runner invokes existing locked reconciler and store seams and adds no retry, cache, snapshot, or composed check-then-act store mutation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Packaged Python is the sole runner-neutral orchestration implementation; no repository-local runner script is required.\n- [ ] `rebar.bridge_run(profile=..., repo_root=...)` exposes the operation through the public Python library and returns captured structured output without writing streams.\n- [ ] `rebar bridge run --profile ...` exposes the same operation through the installed CLI and renders captured streams once.\n- [ ] MCP exposes the same operation as a typed write-gated tool, blocked by read-only mode and requiring Jira-sync authorization.\n- [ ] The wheel contains the runner core and proves availability from pip, Homebrew wheel-backed, and MCP Registry/uvx install shapes.\n- [ ] Explicit `repo_root` overrides inherited `REBAR_ROOT`; installed CLI use outside a repository honors configured `REBAR_ROOT`.\n- [ ] All five existing provider `MODE` values remain accepted and map to the specified legacy or canonical routes.\n- [ ] Public help, library, MCP, schemas, and docs use `profile`; provider configuration retains `MODE` compatibility.\n- [ ] Direct legacy reconcile callers retain published benign results 3/4/75.\n- [ ] The runner translates legacy benign results to canonical 0 while preserving operational 1 and invalid-invocation 2.\n- [ ] Exact valid pause markers skip delivery and return success; malformed markers do not silently pause.\n- [ ] Every successful non-paused pass invokes strict delivery with run id, bot identity, and `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH=always`; delivery failure returns 1 with diagnostics.\n- [ ] A shallow repository returns invalid invocation before reconciliation.\n- [ ] GitHub Actions, Jenkins, and GitLab invoke exactly `rebar bridge run`; GitHub keeps the 20-minute schedule and optional continuous redispatch.\n- [ ] Provider wrappers are schema-validated and their embedded shell passes the pinned ShellCheck; missing or mismatched tooling fails validation.\n- [ ] GitLab schema provenance records and verifies an immutable upstream revision and checksum.\n- [ ] Copied-workflow migration documentation requires atomic workflow and package-pin refresh, while old workflows on old pins remain supported.\n- [ ] Existing workflow, policy, partial-clone, identity, legacy compatibility, library, CLI, and MCP tests remain green.\n- [ ] No new ADR is added; therefore no ADR number or index entry is required.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"pin and verify provider shell validation"},{"path":".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml","reason":"thin GitHub provider wrapper using installed CLI"},{"path":".github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.json","reason":"vendored official GitLab Draft-07 schema"},{"path":".github/schemas/gitlab-ci.schema.provenance.json","reason":"immutable schema provenance and checksum"},{"path":".gitlab-ci.yml","reason":"native GitLab provider wrapper"},{"path":"Jenkinsfile","reason":"native Jenkins provider wrapper"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"release-facing compatibility summary"},{"path":"README.md","reason":"cross-surface and install-path usage"},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"generated CLI reference for bridge run"},{"path":"docs/jira-sync-setup.md","reason":"copied-template install and rollback continuity"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"generated MCP bridge_run reference"},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"portable runner release notes"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"public library bridge_run contract"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"CLI library MCP and legacy compatibility usage"},{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"exact ShellCheck development dependency"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"locked ShellCheck dependency"},{"path":"scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py","reason":"classify write-gated bridge_run tool"},{"path":"src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py","reason":"packaged runner-neutral orchestration core"},{"path":"src/rebar/__init__.py","reason":"public library export"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py","reason":"installed CLI bridge run surface"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge.txt","reason":"canonical profile vocabulary help"},{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_ops.py","reason":"public library facade"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"typed MCP run route"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"write-gated MCP bridge_run tool"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"bridge_run output schema registry"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/bridge_run.schema.json","reason":"shared run result contract"},{"path":"src/rebar/types.py","reason":"public BridgeRun type route"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py","reason":"happy cross-surface bridge_run contracts"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_heldout.py","reason":"held-out signature and MCP gate contracts"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_runner_install_paths_heldout.py","reason":"held-out pip Homebrew MCP wheel and root precedence coverage"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","reason":"exhaustive canonical MCP schema registration"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_reconcile_workflow_no_shallow_rebase.py","reason":"full-history provider delegation continuity"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_reconcile_bridge_push_retry.py","reason":"strict delivery executable smoke coverage"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py","reason":"happy runner routes and delivery oracle"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge_heldout.py","reason":"held-out exit pause error and shallow contracts"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_primary_workflow_heldout.py","reason":"thin primary wrapper compatibility"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers_heldout.py","reason":"held-out provider schema shell and environment parity"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py","reason":"provider ordering schema and ShellCheck contracts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2db2-3f5e-cf3a-464c"],["relates_to","2b38-f76e-99eb-4d7d"],["relates_to","cf7d-fbf8-bd99-49e4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2db2-3f5e-cf3a-464c","parent_status_uuid":"411a9c4b-f062-4397-a6f6-95a13edb5eab","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["bridge","portability","ci"],"ticket_id":"8b08-e4d7-8dca-4aa6","ticket_type":"task","title":"Extract a runner-neutral bridge entrypoint and thin CI wrappers","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9a7d7d9b-393b-4b09-9391-55bef0edd791","7cec6649-4856-48b2-a67a-bf569890279d","0996a487-ad1f-4e37-9653-399052476a9f","411a9c4b-f062-4397-a6f6-95a13edb5eab","7b344e01-07d6-460e-a2fe-0d44125a9acf","fc51064e-0609-4bed-a0a9-1ca273b13fe0","14e9d712-2897-428a-9576-208c630394da","e8eb3bd7-9cf0-42e5-a9ad-872cb92a0f10","36eb56d1-3f16-44b7-8232-4190898d87b7","fb5d9078-a7f1-44c0-a301-4cb254e79bb9","9480d522-8a0d-43f0-8e07-ee8a2f0f7bc9","6f3b28b4-31f3-4830-8ef5-9a4d96c7fff0","43dfc11a-9ebd-459c-96ef-ffa7ef11cb95","12554d17-f1c4-46db-aa69-6f227281cc94","5fe79022-ed58-4e6a-a88f-be371a81803e","56b4efb4-996c-4194-b037-4f3234d02942"]},"env_